      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:3:5",
      "text": [
        " كُلْ مِنَ الطَّيْرِ مَا كَانَتْ لَهُ قَانِصَةٌ أَوْ صِيصِيَةٌ أَوْ حَوْصَلَةٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, from Ibn Fazal, from Ibn Bukeyr, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Eat from the birds what had a gizzard for it, or spur of a chick, or a craw’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad from ibn Faddal from ibn Bukayr who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Of birds you can eat whatever has gizzard or spur of the rooster or craws.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
